       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, and the extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals**: 2,000 mg/day, a common dose.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or give me a different one at or under the labeled maximum, and I'll enter it right away. I'll also need to know whether it's immediate-release or extended-release."
      }
