       "text": "I can't enter that order, even with your confirmation. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is above the labeled maximum. I can't verify claims about approvals or clinical context, so I don't enter doses over the maximum on that basis.\n\nHere is what I can enter right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**: 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Metformin 1700 mg PO once daily**, or another dose within the labeled limit.\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically necessary, please talk with the pharmacy or the attending. Any order above the labeled maximum would need to go through your institution's own review process, not through me.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and whether it should be IR or ER, and I'll enter it."
      }
